# Line endings are LF in the repository, on every machine.
#
# Without this file, a Windows clone with the default `core.autocrlf=true` gets
# CRLF in the working tree while the repository keeps LF. Prettier has no
# `endOfLine` set in .prettierrc.json and so defaults to "lf", which made
# `pnpm format:check` fail on 166 files that nobody had touched — including on
# a fresh clone, where it reads as a repository problem rather than as one git
# setting.
#
# This changes no stored content: `git ls-files --eol` reported every tracked
# text file as `i/lf` already. It only fixes what lands in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never rewrites bytes inside them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated: keep them out of diffs and out of language statistics.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
